==Dialogue==
{{Stub Dialogue}}
===Return to Amphoreus{{subst:void|<!--104060901-->}}===
{{Mission Description|type=trailblaze|location=The Holy City Lost to Time|Okhema, the last city, was a cradle of countless myths.<br />Once, she was like an innocent nymph, sheltered by law, draped in flowing finery, basking in sky's dawning light. She danced across the earth, listened to the ocean's songs, followed reason's teachings, slipped past suitors' trickery, untouched by strife or death. Through ever more beautiful passages she wandered, and people supported her in her worldbearing...<br />Until time took her joy, her beauty, her life, and more. A skeleton lies quietly in a stone coffin. Yet beneath ribs carved like white jade, her heart hasn't withered.<br />Wipe away the dust from that beautiful heart, and listen... listen to the heartbeat preserved for you.}}
{{Dialogue Start}}
----
:{{tx}}
{{Dialogue End}}

===Investigate the anomaly in the spirit basin{{subst:void|<!--104060902-->}}===
{{Dialogue Start}}

:{{DIcon|Изучение}} Investigate
:'''(Trailblazer):''' The Chronocognitive Anchor?
:'''???:''' There's so much I wanted to say for our reunion, yet now that you're back, there's only one thing to say...
:'''???:''' Welcome back, (Trailblazer).
:'''Cyrene:''' It's been such a long, long time.
:{{Диалог|Стрелка}} Cyrene! I'm so glad you're still here...
:{{Диалог|Стрелка}} What happened to the world while I was gone?
:{{Диалог|Стрелка}} I saw March 7th, and she looked really weird.
:'''Cyrene:''' You must be really confused right now, aren't you, (Trailblazer)? So much has happened in Amphoreus while you were gone.
:{{tx}}
{{Dialogue End}}

===(Optional) Investigate the Fragments of Recollection here{{subst:void|<!--104060924-->}}===
{{Dialogue Start}}

:{{DIcon|Разговор}} Listen
----
:'''Herta:''' Hey kiddo, can you see me? Don't bother responding, this is a pre-recorded video message.
:'''Herta:''' Thanks to that little empress granting access to the Ultimate Protocol, Screwy and I... rewrote the progress of "Era Nova" while you were away.
:'''Herta:''' My guess is you don't have much time to listen to all those complicated principles right now, so let me break it down into simple terms that anyone can understand...
:'''Herta:''' Amphoreus has been racing down the Path of Destruction for too long, and the underlying logic of "Era Nova" has been completely corrupted. Screwy and I put in a lot of effort, but we could barely manage to overwrite a small portion of its logic...
:'''Herta:''' Let's take the progress bar as an example. Irontomb's progress bar is currently at 99.98%, and through this rewritten "Era Nova," we're confident we can push it back to 96%... Hmm, let's be conservative, say 97%.
:'''Herta:''' This is a critical matter. The internal structure of the Scepter is too unstable, and we don't know what complications might suddenly arise. The most rational course of action is to quickly run another extrapolation to buy the cosmos a bit more time.
:'''Herta:''' Once you've dealt with that troubling old Intellitron, don't hesitate and start the next cycle of extrapolation right away. Screwy said that "Era Nova" isn't a process that happens in an instant, and the protected nodes of the Scepter are probably at their most vulnerable only during the reset&mdash;
:'''Herta:''' Only by initiating this progress first can we seize the opportunity to make our move. It's all up to you now, "Deliverer."

